@startuml
title Configuration (Assembly Pattern)

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Reify (make explicit) the wiring/assembly of objects forming a composite/complex structure
(often via configuration/metadata/DI).

**Also known as**:
Dependency Injection configuration, Object Composition configuration

**Motivation**:
Externalize composition rules; switch wiring without recompiling.

**Applicability**:
Systems with complex graphs; need runtime/environment-specific assembly.

**Participants**:
Configuration holds definitions.
Configurator reads config and assembles components/composites.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Flexible assembly; environment-driven behavior; testability.
Cons: Complexity; debugging wiring; requires validation.

**Implementation Notes**:
YAML/JSON/XML config; DI containers (Spring, Guice).
Validation and schema for configs.

**Known Uses**:
Spring ApplicationContext XML/Java config; Kubernetes manifests (composing resources).

**Related Patterns**:
Composite, Builder, Facade, Service Locator (avoid), Strategy.

endlegend

interface Component {
  +operation()
}

class Leaf
class Composite {
  +add(c: Component)
  +operation()
}

class Configuration <<data>> {
  +definitions
}

class Configurator {
  +build(config: Configuration) : Component
}

Component <|.. Leaf
Component <|.. Composite
Composite *-- Component : children
Configurator ..> Configuration : reads
Configurator ..> Composite : assembles
@enduml